## How to Test the Code

Follow these instructions to run and verify the codebase on Windows.

### 1. Set Up the Terminal Environment
Navigate to the project root and activate the Python virtual environment:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\SUMIT\Downloads\dev-tool\local-daemon-tool
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### 2. Run Automated Tests
We use `pytest` for unit and integration testing. Run this command to execute all tests:
```powershell
pytest -v
```
You should see output indicating that all 10 tests passed:
* `tests/test_api.py` (4 API integration tests)
* `tests/test_engine.py` (6 engine unit and watchdog tests)

### 3. Start the Server Locally
To run the local daemon server:
```powershell
python -m codeengine.cli
```
This starts the server on `http://localhost:8000` with hot-reloading enabled.

### 4. Manually Test endpoints via PowerShell
Open a separate PowerShell window and run these commands to test the REST API:

#### A. Search for Code (Ripgrep wrapper)
```powershell
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/search/code?q=print&path=.&lang=python" -Method Get
```

#### B. Find Files (FD wrapper)
```powershell
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/search/file?pattern=app&root=." -Method Get
```

#### C. Extract Function AST Source
```powershell
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/search/function?file=codeengine/app.py&name=startup" -Method Get
```

#### D. Preview a Code Edit (Unified Diff)
```powershell
$body = @{
    file = "codeengine/app.py"
    old_code = "app = FastAPI(title=`"Code Search Engine`", version=`"1.0.0`")"
    new_code = "app = FastAPI(title=`"Antigravity Code Search Engine`", version=`"1.0.0`")"
} | ConvertTo-Json

$preview = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/preview-edit" -Method Post -Body $body -ContentType "application/json"
$preview | Format-List
```

#### E. Apply the Edit (Writes to file + Git commits)
```powershell
$applyBody = @{
    edit_id = $preview.edit_id
} | ConvertTo-Json

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/apply-edit" -Method Post -Body $applyBody -ContentType "application/json"
```

#### F. Undo the Last Edit (Git revert HEAD)
```powershell
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8000/undo" -Method Post
```
